## Documentation-derived question content

The question corpus in `data/` is derived from the Cilium project's
documentation, which is licensed **Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International (CC BY 4.0)**. The code of the Cilium project is Apache-2.0; the
documentation is CC BY 4.0 under section 11 of the CNCF charter and the
dual-licence notice published on <https://cilium.io>.

- **Source repository:** <https://github.com/cilium/cilium>
- **Pinned reference:** `v1.20.4` (released 2026-10-23)
- **Source path:** `Documentation/`
- **Copyright:** The Cilium Authors
- **Licence:** CC BY 4.0 — <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>

Every generated question carries an exact citation of the form
`file.rst#heading-anchor`, which resolves to a URL under
<https://docs.cilium.io/en/stable/>. The `data/sources.json` file records the
commit that was used, the retrieval date, and the byte counts.

### What this repository does NOT contain

- No question content from commercial exam-dump sites.
- No content from the Isovalent CCA Study Guide, which is CC BY-NC 4.0
  (non-commercial) and is therefore incompatible with unrestricted
  redistribution.
- No questions from the Linux Foundation CCA exam itself. Exam items are
  confidential under the Linux Foundation Global Certification and
  Confidentiality Agreement.

### Held-out evaluation set

`data/blind-set.json` contains questions from the public CNCF practice-exam
repository at <https://gitlab.com/cncf-exams/certified-cillium-associate-cca>.
It is used only for blind self-assessment and is excluded from the practising
corpus. Check that project's terms before redistributing it.
